.SH FEATURE AVAILABILITY
.B dsnap
selects one package manager at compile time. The
.BR apt ,
.BR dnf ,
and
.B pacman
features are mutually exclusive. The generated command list reflects the
features selected for the build, so unavailable feature-gated commands are
not shown.
.TP
.B base-import
The
.B base-import
command is compiled in only with the
.B base-import
feature.
.TP
.B import
The
.B import
command is compiled in only with the
.B import
feature.
.TP
.B fixdb
The
.B fixdb
command is compiled in only with the
.B pacman
feature. In dnf and apt builds it reports that the subcommand is not
supported rather than attempting pacman keyring repair.
.SH NOTES
.B efi-update
requires an EFI firmware interface. Without
.IR /sys/firmware/efi ,
for example inside WSL, it reports that the command is not supported.
.PP
Commands that operate on snapshot copies normally create a locked
.I snapshot-chrN
working subvolume. If a command is interrupted, use
.B dsnap unlock -s N
to clear the lock and discard the uncommitted changes.
.PP
The
.B auto-upgrade
service and timer shipped with dsnap are inert by default and are never
enabled automatically.
.PP
Time synchronization accepts a clock only when at least two verified HTTPS
sources agree within ten seconds. Local clock helpers are unauthenticated and
are disabled by default. If explicitly enabled, they are only a bootstrap and
must still be confirmed by verified HTTPS before dsnap proceeds.
.PP
Shells and commands entered through dsnap run in a private mount namespace,
prefer
.BR pivot_root (2)
with a chroot fallback, drop unnecessary root capabilities, install a seccomp
denylist, and set
.BR no_new_privs .
Optional AppArmor or SELinux transitions can be requested with the environment
variables below; a configured transition must succeed or the command is denied.
User namespaces are not used because dsnap operates on root-owned host
filesystems; a user namespace without a full UID map would break package
management, and a full map would not provide a meaningful boundary.
.PP
The live recovery shell intentionally keeps the shared
.I /var
mount. It no longer exposes the host's full
.IR /dev ,
.IR /run ,
or
.I /tmp .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DSNAP_APPARMOR_PROFILE
If set, dsnap asks AppArmor to transition the chroot shell or command to this
profile before execution. The profile must already be loaded.
.TP
.B DSNAP_SELINUX_CONTEXT
If set, dsnap asks SELinux to transition the chroot shell or command to this
context before execution. The context must already be valid on the system.
.TP
.B DSNAP_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED_TIME_SYNC
Set to
.BR 1 ,
.BR true ,
or
.B yes
to allow unauthenticated local clock helpers as a bootstrap when verified
HTTPS time is unavailable. Local helpers never establish trusted time by
themselves.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully, or an informational command printed its
state.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, a requested snapshot or path does not exist, or an
operation was rejected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dsnap/export-keys
Root-owned public keys trusted for verifying signed snapshot exports.
.TP
.I /.snapshots
Btrfs filesystem holding dsnap snapshot subvolumes and metadata.
.TP
.I /.snapshots/dsnap/fstree
Serialized snapshot tree.
.TP
.I /.snapshots/dsnap/snapshots/N-desc
Description of snapshot
.IR N .
.TP
.I /.snapshots/dsnap/upstate
Last update status and date.
.TP
.I /.snapshots/rootfs/snapshot-N
Root filesystem subvolume for snapshot
.IR N .
.TP
.I /.snapshots/boot/boot-N
Boot directory subvolume for snapshot
.IR N .
.TP
.I /.snapshots/etc/etc-N
Configuration subvolume for snapshot
.IR N .
.TP
.I /.snapshots/var/var-N
Variable data subvolume for snapshot
.IR N .
.TP
.I /usr/share/dsnap/snap
File containing the current snapshot number.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dsnap/deploy
File containing the active deployment slot.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dsnap/profiles
Installed dsnap profiles.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the snapshot tree and current snapshot:
.PP
.nf
.RS
dsnap tree
dsnap current
.RE
.fi
.PP
Upgrade snapshot 1 noninteractively and make it the next boot target:
.PP
.nf
.RS
dsnap upgrade -s 1 -y
dsnap deploy -s 1
.RE
.fi
.PP
Create a described child of the current snapshot:
.PP
.nf
.RS
dsnap add-branch -d "test snapshot"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Export the base snapshot to a directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
dsnap export -s 0 -o /var/tmp -k <GPG_KEY_ID>
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR btrfs-subvolume (8),
.BR grub-mkconfig (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
